Two-Headed Giant (Commander Duels v0.5.1 card audit): the cards the audit fixed one by one.

Reason: the cards whose own code reads one active player, one attacking player or one player's poison
counters, where part 3's rules do not reach. In a team game (Game.getTeammates, from part 1):
- "your turn" compared with the active player by id reads the team's turn (805.9: Game.isActivePlayer);
- custom triggers worded for "each player's" step and "that player" trigger for each player of the
  active team, and a few "each player's" triggers built as "each step" say so (805.4d:
  triggersForEachTeamPlayer, withTriggersForEachTeamPlayer);
- watchers that record the beginning of a turn record it for each player of the active team;
- "you attack with" counts the creatures you control, and "that attacking player" is the one
  attacking the enchanted player (805.10a, 805.10c);
- effects that check a player's poison counters count the team's (810.10a), and Melira, Sylvok
  Outcast keeps the whole team from getting them (810.10c);
- Biorhythm, Shaman of Forgotten Ways and Reverse the Sands set or redistribute one life total per
  team (810.9d, 810.9f).
docs/engine/two-headed-giant-audit.csv in Commander Duels lists every card reviewed and its verdict.
Every other game type names no teammates, and each change reduces to the card's own code there.
Needs parts 1 and 3.
Upstream: none yet; to be offered to magefree/mage with the other parts.
Remove when: XMage upstream implements Two-Headed Giant, or the format is dropped.

